  "conclusion": "Two runs with a run-level offset that share the condition pattern (rule R2 passes). Offset evidence: a series built from a random member of each pair is much rougher (median residual SD 2.42 over 73 cells) than the hi series (1.14), the lo series (0.61) or the pair means (0.75), as expected if each cell holds two smooth runs at different levels. The per-pair median hi/lo (2.29) is >= 1 by construction, so it is weak evidence on its own. Shared pattern: median Spearman(hi, lo) 0.436 vs null-A 95th percentile of the median 0.054; 45 of 85 cells individually exceed their own null-A 95th percentile, the rest are not individually distinguishable from null A."
